      "description": "PaliCAD is a lightweight 3D CAD app for iPad and iPhone.\n\nCreate, edit, and refine 3D models with a straightforward direct-modeling workflow. PaliCAD combines 2D sketching, solid modeling, analysis tools, and support for common CAD file formats in an interface designed to work naturally with touch and supports the Apple Pencil on iPad and iPhone Duo.\n\nPaliCAD is actively developed and growing. Version 1.0 is aimed at makers, hobbyists, and CAD enthusiasts who value an affordable lightweight, offline modelling tool capable of managing simple to moderately complex designs.\n\nPaliCAD is built around a simple idea: CAD software should be capable, cross-platform, lightweight, offline, and financially accessible without requiring an ongoing subscription.\n\nKEY FEATURES\n• Non-parametric direct 3D modeling\n • 2D sketching with a straightforward sketch-to-extrude workflow \n• 3D Boolean operations for combining, subtracting, and intersecting solids \n• Fillets and chamfers for refining edges \n• Import of image references \n• Joints for visualizing basic part movement \n• Section analysis for inspecting internal geometry \n• Import and export support for common CAD file formats\n • Save projects in PaliCAD's native cross-platform .pali project format \n• Customizable light and dark themes \n• Customizable keyboard shortcuts for faster workflows\n\nOne time purchase. No subscriptions.\n\nModels you create with PaliCAD are yours to use, including for personal and commercial purposes. PaliCAD places no additional licensing restrictions on the models you create. As always, third-party files, images, designs, or other material you import remain subject to their respective rights and licenses.\n\nPaliCAD and it’s underlying CAD kernel are actively evolving projects. New modelling tools, workflow improvements, and compatibility enhancements will continue to be developed over time.\n\nOPEN DEVELOPMENT\n\nAt its core is Pali Ijo, an open-source CAD kernel released under the permissive MIT License. Pali Ijo is developed as a separate project so its geometry and modelling tools can be shared with everyone.",
